# Lavaleaper: "Whenever a player taps a basic land for mana, that player adds one mana of any type that land produced"
# (CR 106.12a, 605.1b, 605.4a) and "All creatures have haste" (CR 702.10, 613.1f). Turn 1: Bot1's Mountain, tapped before
# Lavaleaper is out, gives {R} alone; Lavaleaper (paid with Black Lotus) attacks the turn it arrives. Turn 2: Bot2 - "a
# player", "that player" - taps its basic Island for {U}{U} into its own pool (Bot1's stays empty), casts Snapcaster Mage
# with it, and the Mage attacks at once under Bot1's Lavaleaper (still tapped from its attack). Turn 3: Bayou, a Swamp
# Forest but not basic (CR 205.4c), taps for {B} alone, the control; then Bot1's basic Mountain taps for {R}{R} - the {B}
# already in the pool is no mana the Mountain produced, so there is no choice of type to make (`! Bot1.Modes`).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Lavaleaper
Bayou
Mountain x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Snapcaster Mage
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Lavaleaper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T1 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Lavaleaper)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
? Bot2.Mana = {U}{U}
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot2.Hand.Snapcaster Mage.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Snapcaster Mage)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Bayou.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Bayou.Activate(Ability: {B})
? Bot1.Mana = {B}
! Bot1.Modes
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {B}{R}{R}

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Snapcaster Mage
